#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""Bridge between the Mac Menu Bridge browser extension and KDE's global menu.

Publishes Vivaldi-style menus as com.canonical.dbusmenu at /MenuBar and marks
Vivaldi's X11 windows with that address, so the stock Global Menu widget
shows them (Vivaldi must run via XWayland). Clicks become commands for the
extension, or keyboard shortcuts when it isn't connected.

The extension connects to ws://127.0.0.1:PORT and proves itself with a shared
token (~/.config/vivaldi-menu-bridge/config.json). The Plasma widget talks to
this process over D-Bus:

    org.brhett.VivaldiMenu  /org/brhett/VivaldiMenu
      Command(s name, s argsJson)      run a browser command (or "keys")
      Query(s what) -> s json          history, bookmarks, tabs, recentlyClosed
      Connected() -> b                 whether the extension is connected

"keys" commands are typed with ydotool for things extensions can't do
(clipboard, find, print, developer tools).
"""
